nvmap: load on Tegra210 and return handles as file descriptors

R35's loadable nvmap refuses to load unless the chip is Tegra186 or newer.
Accept nvidia,tegra210 too, and build with NVMAP_CONFIG_HANDLE_AS_FD=y:
R32's nvmap, which JetPack 4's libraries were built against, returns
handles as file descriptors, where R35 defaults to plain IDs.

Tested on the Nano: CUDA 10.2 passed every test under 5.10 in trial 11.

Licence: GPL-2.0-only. Lab notes, with every measurement: NOTES.md.
---
diff --git a/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/Makefile.memory.configs b/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/Makefile.memory.configs
index 2eb230b0b..9f7901d20 100644
--- a/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/Makefile.memory.configs
+++ b/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/Makefile.memory.configs
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ NVMAP_CONFIG_DEBUG_MAPS := n
 # This is fallback option to support handle as FD
 # To support handle as ID, set this to n
 # This config is useful to debug issue if its due to handle as ID or FD
-NVMAP_CONFIG_HANDLE_AS_FD := n
+NVMAP_CONFIG_HANDLE_AS_FD := y
 
 # Config for kstable/OOT kernel
 # This is useful when any kstable/OOT specific checks are needed
diff --git a/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/nvmap_init.c b/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/nvmap_init.c
index f5279723d..2b1628654 100644
--- a/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/nvmap_init.c
+++ b/nvidia/drivers/video/tegra/nvmap/nvmap_init.c
@@ -935,7 +935,8 @@ static int __init nvmap_init_driver(void)
 		goto fail;
 
 #ifdef NVMAP_LOADABLE_MODULE
-	if (!(of_machine_is_compatible("nvidia,tegra186") ||
+	if (!(of_machine_is_compatible("nvidia,tegra210") ||
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("nvidia,tegra186") ||
 	    of_machine_is_compatible("nvidia,tegra194") ||
 	    of_machine_is_compatible("nvidia,tegra234") ||
 	    of_machine_is_compatible("nvidia,tegra239") ||
